### [09:52:40 UTC] Step 5 — Spectral analysis of output_test.flac
Input: output_test.flac vs input_test.flac vs a pure 7x zero-order-hold (np.repeat) of the decoded input_test.mp3.
Action: Ran scratchpad/analyze.py (STFT nperseg=2048/noverlap=1024, 32-band mean-magnitude comparison, clipping/dropout/discontinuity/noise-floor checks) plus a targeted ZOH-baseline comparison script.
Reasoning: Rules step 5 — look for clipping, dropouts, discontinuities, artifacts, and whether added detail is real.
Output: Clean on every hygiene check: 0 NaN/Inf; clipping fraction 1.693e-04 in output, identical 1.693e-04 in reference; 0 dropout runs >50 ms in either file; discontinuity 99.9th pct 0.0581817 (out) vs 0.0581818 (ref), ratio 0.999998; noise-floor p10 -145.47 dB in both (rise 0.00 dB - the previously reported +6.12 dB IST noise-floor rise is gone). Band deltas out-vs-ref are 0.00 dB in all 32 bands (0-154.35 kHz).
ARTIFACT FOUND: the output's entire above-22.05 kHz content is zero-order-hold imaging, not reconstructed detail - spectral images centered at 44.1/88.2/132.3 kHz with nulls at ~22/66/110/154 kHz (the classic 7x sample-and-hold sinc pattern), levels -76 to -136 dB. 99.99% of the output's 7-sample groups are bit-identical internally, and corr(output, pure np.repeat(mp3_samples,7)) = 0.9999999999841 with max abs diff 2.09e-06 - i.e. IST + autoscale + normalize + LMS adaptive filter together change the waveform by <2.1e-06 versus plain sample-and-hold. Root cause candidates for generate-code: (a) IST harmonic amplitude is now 0.1/max_iter = 3.3e-04 and the IST result is added to an unnormalized expanded channel, so its contribution vanishes after peak normalization; (b) lms_filter() is now an exact identity - upscale() calls lms_filter(channel, channel), and with w[0]=1.0 the output y == signal[i] makes the error e identically 0, so the weights never adapt, yet this no-op consumes ~18-19 of the run's 19.6 minutes.
REFERENCE-DEGENERACY FOUND: input_test.flac is itself a 7x zero-order-hold of input_test.mp3 (corr 0.9999999999999926, max abs diff 2.38e-07, 87.6% of 7-sample groups internally identical), not an independent high-resolution ground truth. Grading against it therefore cannot detect missing added detail.

